  "questions": [
    {
      "numero": "a",
      "enonce_markdown": "(a) the value of the constant $k$.",
      "corrige_markdown": "The probabilities must sum to 1:\n\n| $x$ | 0 | 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 | 5 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| $f(x)$ | $6k$ | $5k$ | $4k$ | $3k$ | $2k$ | $k$ |\n\n$$\\sum f(x) = k(6 + 5 + 4 + 3 + 2 + 1) = 21k = 1$$\n\n**$k = \\dfrac{1}{21}$.**",
      "themes": [
        "discrete random variables statistics"
      ],
      "difficulte_estimee": "faible",
      "type_reponse": "ouverte",
      "choix": [],
      "reponse_correcte": "",
      "points": 3
    },
    {
      "numero": "b",
      "enonce_markdown": "(b) the mean of $X$.",
      "corrige_markdown": "$$E(X) = \\sum x f(x) = k(0 \\cdot 6 + 1 \\cdot 5 + 2 \\cdot 4 + 3 \\cdot 3 + 4 \\cdot 2 + 5 \\cdot 1) = k(5 + 8 + 9 + 8 + 5) = 35k = \\frac{35}{21}$$\n\n**$E(X) = \\dfrac{5}{3} \\approx 1.67$.**",
      "themes": [
        "expectation and variance",
        "discrete random variables statistics"
      ],
      "difficulte_estimee": "faible",
      "type_reponse": "ouverte",
      "choix": [],
      "reponse_correcte": "",
      "points": 3
    },
    {
      "numero": "c",
      "enonce_markdown": "(c) the variance of $X$.",
      "corrige_markdown": "$$E(X^2) = \\sum x^2 f(x) = k(0 + 1 \\cdot 5 + 4 \\cdot 4 + 9 \\cdot 3 + 16 \\cdot 2 + 25 \\cdot 1) = k(5 + 16 + 27 + 32 + 25) = 105k = \\frac{105}{21} = 5$$\n\n$$\\operatorname{Var}(X) = E(X^2) - [E(X)]^2 = 5 - \\left(\\frac{5}{3}\\right)^2 = 5 - \\frac{25}{9} = \\frac{20}{9}$$\n\n**$\\operatorname{Var}(X) = \\dfrac{20}{9} \\approx 2.22$.**",
      "themes": [
        "expectation and variance"
      ],
      "difficulte_estimee": "moyenne",
      "type_reponse": "ouverte",
      "choix": [],
      "reponse_correcte": "",
      "points": 3
    },
    {
      "numero": "d",
      "enonce_markdown": "Another random variable $Y$ is such that $Y = 4X + 5$. Find\n\n(d) the mean of $Y$",
      "corrige_markdown": "For $Y = aX + b$, $E(Y) = aE(X) + b$.\n\n$$E(Y) = 4 \\times \\frac{5}{3} + 5 = \\frac{20}{3} + \\frac{15}{3} = \\frac{35}{3}$$\n\n**$E(Y) = \\dfrac{35}{3} \\approx 11.67$.**",
      "themes": [
        "expectation and variance"
      ],
      "difficulte_estimee": "faible",
      "type_reponse": "ouverte",
      "choix": [],
      "reponse_correcte": "",
      "points": 2
    },
    {
      "numero": "e",
      "enonce_markdown": "(e) the variance of $Y$",
      "corrige_markdown": "For $Y = aX + b$, $\\operatorname{Var}(Y) = a^2 \\operatorname{Var}(X)$ (the constant $b$ shifts the distribution without changing its spread).\n\n$$\\operatorname{Var}(Y) = 4^2 \\times \\frac{20}{9} = \\frac{320}{9}$$\n\n**$\\operatorname{Var}(Y) = \\dfrac{320}{9} \\approx 35.56$.**",
